2991
02:12:03.270 --> 02:12:04.630
And I've been there for two years.

2992
02:12:04.630 --> 02:12:08.100
So, I'll have been there when you're there.

2993
02:12:08.100 --> 02:12:10.307
And then six months later, I'll be like,

2994
02:12:10.307 --> 02:12:11.950
"Wait, are you married to?"

2995
02:12:11.950 --> 02:12:13.540
And so, I'll hear your wife's side of the story

2996
02:12:13.540 --> 02:12:14.890
and then I'll hear your kid's side of the story.

2997
02:12:14.890 --> 02:12:18.997
So, I have a lot of this information in my head

2998
02:12:18.997 --> 02:12:21.390
and I go, oh, wow. Like this is a lot.

2999
02:12:21.390 --> 02:12:26.390
And I feel like all the things that I do of helping people,

3000
02:12:28.170 --> 02:12:30.193
donating money and my time it's like,

3001
02:12:32.048 --> 02:12:34.660
it's like, oh, you give a home...

3002
02:12:34.660 --> 02:12:35.897
I'm like, "Oh, I'll give a homeless guy some money

3003
02:12:35.897 --> 02:12:36.833
and some clothes and some food.

3004
02:12:36.833 --> 02:12:41.070
He's like, he's not making light of what I did.

3005
02:12:41.070 --> 02:12:42.890
I helped him for that day for that moment.

3006
02:12:42.890 --> 02:12:44.810
But did that get to the root of it?

3007
02:12:44.810 --> 02:12:46.680
Did that get the brokenness?

3008
02:12:46.680 --> 02:12:49.310
And I go, "How can I...

3009
02:12:50.940 --> 02:12:54.900
It's like, as someone who has privilege, who has wealth,

3010
02:12:54.900 --> 02:12:59.240
like what is my best way to serve myself and humanity

3011
02:12:59.240 --> 02:13:03.690
and help one another cause you get to...

3012
02:13:06.410 --> 02:13:09.080
When we had Trump as president, like, man, fuck this guy's.

3013
02:13:09.080 --> 02:13:10.464
He's a horrible.

3014
02:13:10.464 --> 02:13:12.210
And it's like, you know just as well,

3015
02:13:12.210 --> 02:13:14.260
there's a broken child in there.

3016
02:13:14.260 --> 02:13:16.510
There's a hurt child in there.

3017
02:13:16.510 --> 02:13:21.430
And is there any place in our culture for a guy,

3018
02:13:21.430 --> 02:13:23.207
if he woke up the next day and was like,

3019
02:13:23.207 --> 02:13:25.633
"Man, I've messed up. I wanna change."

3020
02:13:25.633 --> 02:13:26.860
It's like, "No."

3021
02:13:26.860 --> 02:13:28.310
It's just kill that guy.

3022
02:13:28.310 --> 02:13:29.610
Like down with him.

3023
02:13:29.610 --> 02:13:32.320
And so, it's so polarizing.

3024
02:13:32.320 --> 02:13:36.360
And even with myself, you get into any treatment,

3025
02:13:36.360 --> 02:13:39.060
you go to narcotics anonymous and it's like,

3026
02:13:39.060 --> 02:13:40.692
there's a hierarchy, right?

3027
02:13:40.692 --> 02:13:42.630
It's like, oh, well, we're into opioids

3028
02:13:42.630 --> 02:13:44.190
and all you do is smoke weed.

3029
02:13:44.190 --> 02:13:47.440
And oh, I had more trauma than you and this and that.

3030
02:13:47.440 --> 02:13:50.713
And I sit there and I go,

3031
02:13:52.710 --> 02:13:56.210
if there's no room in our culture for redemption and change,

3032
02:13:56.210 --> 02:14:00.370
so as someone who's is like me, who is so judgmental,

3033
02:14:00.370 --> 02:14:03.410
who is a hater, I always try to lead with love.

3034
02:14:03.410 --> 02:14:08.410
And so, I've been asked to do such hard things

3035
02:14:09.650 --> 02:14:10.593
in my recovery.

3036
02:14:13.320 --> 02:14:16.070
There's people that are in recovery.

3037
02:14:16.070 --> 02:14:18.490
I meet murderers and rapists

3038
02:14:18.490 --> 02:14:21.610
and people that are in prison still

3039
02:14:21.610 --> 02:14:24.330
and have done horrendous things,

3040
02:14:24.330 --> 02:14:28.170
who've ripped people off and who should be in prison.

3041
02:14:28.170 --> 02:14:30.820
And so, I'll meet them and I'll be asked to sponsor them.

3042
02:14:30.820 --> 02:14:32.590
I'll be asked to work with them.

3043
02:14:32.590 --> 02:14:34.437
And I go, "Absolutely not.

3044
02:14:34.437 --> 02:14:37.627
"Like I think that person should burn in hell

3045
02:14:37.627 --> 02:14:38.860
"and be in prison."

3046
02:14:38.860 --> 02:14:43.533
And they go, "Can you also help them?

3047
02:14:44.387 --> 02:14:46.293
"Can you want them to burn in prison

3048
02:14:46.293 --> 02:14:48.447
"and hell and also help them?"

3049
02:14:49.520 --> 02:14:51.910
And I go, "Fuck, I gotta think about that."

3050
02:14:51.910 --> 02:14:56.570
Because for you, like if someone's out there

3051
02:14:56.570 --> 02:14:58.420
and they've been a horrible person

3052
02:14:58.420 --> 02:15:01.097
and they should be in prison and yet they're not in prison

3053
02:15:01.097 --> 02:15:04.420
and they're still out and they want to change,

3054
02:15:04.420 --> 02:15:06.900
is shaming them and yelling at them...

3055
02:15:07.920 --> 02:15:10.417
So, I had these experiences where I would meet people

3056
02:15:10.417 --> 02:15:11.750
and I go,

3057
02:15:11.750 --> 02:15:13.557
and I would be able to tell them, I would be like,

3058
02:15:13.557 --> 02:15:16.197
"I feel uncomfortable sitting next to you right now.

3059
02:15:16.197 --> 02:15:17.867
"I know you got out of prison early.

3060
02:15:17.867 --> 02:15:19.637
"I believe you should still be in prison

3061
02:15:19.637 --> 02:15:22.487
"and should be there till you die.

3062
02:15:22.487 --> 02:15:24.367
"And yet because you're not in prison

3063
02:15:24.367 --> 02:15:27.047
"and I'm not judge/jury executioner,

3064
02:15:27.047 --> 02:15:28.657
"I'm willing to work with you

3065
02:15:28.657 --> 02:15:31.460
"if you are serious about changing."

3066
02:15:31.460 --> 02:15:33.748
Because it doesn't help for someone who's like that

3067
02:15:33.748 --> 02:15:34.581
to live in...

3068
02:15:34.581 --> 02:15:37.620
'Cause he's just going to be in society worse.

3069
02:15:37.620 --> 02:15:41.470
And so, as they say, nothing changes if nothing changes.

3070
02:15:41.470 --> 02:15:45.350
I was ready to sail off into the sunset,

3071
02:15:45.350 --> 02:15:46.580
done with podcasting.

3072
02:15:46.580 --> 02:15:48.960
I don't like the anxiety that comes with speaking

3073
02:15:48.960 --> 02:15:50.860
behind a microphone.

3074
02:15:50.860 --> 02:15:52.300
I don't need to be on TV.

3075
02:15:52.300 --> 02:15:54.700
All those real things of why,

3076
02:15:54.700 --> 02:15:57.233
before they took those opportunities away,

3077
02:15:58.730 --> 02:16:00.930
why I did decide...

3078
02:16:00.930 --> 02:16:04.360
What I was deciding whether or not to do TV,

3079
02:16:04.360 --> 02:16:05.750
what I did see in Bordain,

3080
02:16:05.750 --> 02:16:08.720
what I did see what fame and workaholism did to him,

3081
02:16:08.720 --> 02:16:11.847
I was like, "I'll just do the one-on-one thing in private,

3082
02:16:11.847 --> 02:16:14.557
"no cameras. I don't need to broadcast this.

3083
02:16:14.557 --> 02:16:17.740
"I'll just help people the way I help people."

3084
02:16:17.740 --> 02:16:21.360
And but there's the ego. And the workaholism is like,

3085
02:16:21.360 --> 02:16:22.830
but I need to help everyone.

3086
02:16:22.830 --> 02:16:24.040
I gotta help the whole world.

3087
02:16:24.040 --> 02:16:26.670
Like I gotta change everything.

3088
02:16:26.670 --> 02:16:31.290
And I sat in it and I already knew

3089
02:16:31.290 --> 02:16:34.120
that there would be no network that would show that show.

3090
02:16:34.120 --> 02:16:37.330
So, I went ahead and filmed. I made it myself.

3091
02:16:37.330 --> 02:16:41.410
And then FX stepped in and their whole logo is fearless.

3092
02:16:41.410 --> 02:16:42.920
And they set up...

3093
02:16:42.920 --> 02:16:44.770
And they didn't get involved editorially

3094
02:16:44.770 --> 02:16:46.190
with trying to change anything?

3095
02:16:46.190 --> 02:16:49.050
There was a little bit, it was a conversation.

3096
02:16:49.050 --> 02:16:50.070
I took the Louis deal,

3097
02:16:50.070 --> 02:16:54.384
Louis C.K. created, edited, did everything for less money.

3098
02:16:54.384 --> 02:16:55.927
So, I was like, "I'll take that deal.

3099
02:16:55.927 --> 02:16:59.260
"I don't need to get paid. I never did this for the money."

3100
02:16:59.260 --> 02:17:02.360
So, I took less money for more creative control.

3101
02:17:02.360 --> 02:17:05.140
And they were concerned.

3102
02:17:05.140 --> 02:17:07.663
Like no one else would sit down with me.

3103
02:17:09.887 --> 02:17:13.070
Here's the thing that's about the shame and anonymity

3104
02:17:13.070 --> 02:17:18.070
is someone at all those companies knows who I am.

3105
02:17:18.518 --> 02:17:20.327
They're like, "Dude, I love you on Vice. I love Thumbs-up.

3106
02:17:20.327 --> 02:17:21.474
"I love..."

3107
02:17:21.474 --> 02:17:22.326
But we just can't do it.

3108
02:17:22.326 --> 02:17:23.660
And they go, "But we're not gonna work."

3109
02:17:23.660 --> 02:17:25.920
This show comes out, the new show.

3110
02:17:25.920 --> 02:17:28.210
And I have some of the biggest celebrities on the planet

3111
02:17:28.210 --> 02:17:29.043
reach out to me and they were like,

3112
02:17:29.043 --> 02:17:30.737
"Dude, I don't even know who you are,

3113
02:17:30.737 --> 02:17:32.967
"but someone turned your show on.

3114
02:17:32.967 --> 02:17:34.330
"I watched all four episodes."

3115
02:17:34.330 --> 02:17:37.587
And I was like, "Cool, can you be the next guest?

3116
02:17:37.587 --> 02:17:38.420
"Can you tweet about?"

3117
02:17:38.420 --> 02:17:39.740
And they're like, "No, no, no."

3118
02:17:39.740 --> 02:17:40.996
Really?

3119
02:17:40.996 --> 02:17:42.240
"This is just me privately telling you this."

3120
02:17:42.240 --> 02:17:43.540
And I go, "Oh, okay."

3121
02:17:43.540 --> 02:17:46.670
So, that's how deep those things run.

3122
02:17:46.670 --> 02:17:50.800
And I'm forever grateful to everyone at Effects

3123
02:17:50.800 --> 02:17:52.780
'cause they're so cool to work with.

3124
02:17:52.780 --> 02:17:56.040
And they put out all these challenging TV shows

3125
02:17:56.040 --> 02:17:58.790
and stuff with like the antihero.

3126
02:17:58.790 --> 02:18:03.180
And they said, "Listen, we..."

3127
02:18:03.180 --> 02:18:05.127
'Cause of the show was already done.

3128
02:18:05.127 --> 02:18:07.055
They're like, the world needs to see this.

3129
02:18:07.055 --> 02:18:08.003
This is amazing.

3130
02:18:09.570 --> 02:18:12.680
We're just worried that like you might get canceled

3131
02:18:12.680 --> 02:18:15.880
or you have such a crazy history of in saying things

3132
02:18:15.880 --> 02:18:17.210
you've done and said,

3133
02:18:17.210 --> 02:18:19.237
and I was like, "Oh, that what you're worried about?

3134
02:18:19.237 --> 02:18:20.977
"That's easy for...

3135
02:18:20.977 --> 02:18:22.597
"Let me make the decision for you.

3136
02:18:22.597 --> 02:18:24.077
"Hard pass on David Choe."

3137
02:18:26.060 --> 02:18:27.270
And they go, agh.

3138
02:18:29.372 --> 02:18:30.580
And like, didn't you like learn your lesson

3139
02:18:30.580 --> 02:18:32.280
with like Louie and all this other stuff?

3140
02:18:32.280 --> 02:18:34.510
And also, you have a history

3141
02:18:34.510 --> 02:18:36.920
of doing that reverse jujitsu maneuver

3142
02:18:36.920 --> 02:18:38.760
where you take it off the table

3143
02:18:38.760 --> 02:18:40.480
and they want it more.

3144
02:18:40.480 --> 02:18:42.500
I don't know if I was doing, I mean,

3145
02:18:42.500 --> 02:18:43.795
thank you for saying that.

3146
02:18:43.795 --> 02:18:45.020
I mean, that might not have been your motivation,

3147
02:18:45.020 --> 02:18:48.329
but that's the psychological impact of doing that.

3148
02:18:48.329 --> 02:18:50.160
I just wanted to know that everyone had...

3149
02:18:50.160 --> 02:18:53.080
So, I could be clear I'm like everyone has now rejected me.

3150
02:18:53.080 --> 02:18:55.050
So now I can just become a YouTuber.

3151
02:18:55.050 --> 02:18:57.940
I was like, once everyone has said, no...

3152
02:18:57.940 --> 02:19:00.540
And it would have been huge on YouTube if you'd done that.

3153
02:19:00.540 --> 02:19:03.120
I mean, and ultimately that's my, I don't know.

3154
02:19:03.120 --> 02:19:05.130
And maybe more people would have seen it.

3155
02:19:05.130 --> 02:19:07.200
But it always comes back down to this,

3156
02:19:07.200 --> 02:19:10.893
and which is also the hesitancy to come here today is,

3157
02:19:12.230 --> 02:19:15.330
when you do anything like that, outreach, recovery work,

3158
02:19:15.330 --> 02:19:18.020
something where you're putting out a positive message,

3159
02:19:18.020 --> 02:19:19.193
showing change,

3160
02:19:20.610 --> 02:19:22.480
you will help people,

3161
02:19:22.480 --> 02:19:24.995
but then comes with that an expectation.

3162
02:19:24.995 --> 02:19:27.440
And when you spoke earlier about,

3163
02:19:27.440 --> 02:19:28.830
so the show is doing good,

3164
02:19:28.830 --> 02:19:31.320
and it was one of my biggest fears talking to Neil Strauss

3165
02:19:31.320 --> 02:19:34.500
and other, like really smart, brilliant people in recovery

3166
02:19:34.500 --> 02:19:38.550
is going to any of these behavioral places

3167
02:19:38.550 --> 02:19:40.670
and learning about addiction and behavior,

3168
02:19:40.670 --> 02:19:43.960
you're gonna learn all these tools and in the same way,

3169
02:19:43.960 --> 02:19:45.040
like learning the force,

3170
02:19:45.040 --> 02:19:47.420
you can use it for the light or the dark side.

3171
02:19:47.420 --> 02:19:51.080
So, I've met people who are like brilliant in recovery

3172
02:19:51.080 --> 02:19:52.790
and yet their lives are falling apart.

3173
02:19:52.790 --> 02:19:55.530
And they go into this martyr thing

3174
02:19:55.530 --> 02:19:58.270
and like I don't know Tony Robbins,

3175
02:19:58.270 --> 02:19:59.900
but every time I see him speak,

3176
02:19:59.900 --> 02:20:03.570
I'm like, holy shit, this guy is like, brilliant.

3177
02:20:03.570 --> 02:20:07.130
And he's so selfless and helping all these people.

3178
02:20:07.130 --> 02:20:09.770
And he seems like a douche. It's like two things.

3179
02:20:09.770 --> 02:20:13.470
I'm like, "Would I ever wanna be that guy?"

3180
02:20:13.470 --> 02:20:14.640
It's so weird.

3181
02:20:14.640 --> 02:20:16.950
Like he's helping so many people through,

3182
02:20:16.950 --> 02:20:19.910
and that's priceless and that's invaluable. And yet...

3183
02:20:19.910 --> 02:20:21.990
Yeah. But your self-awareness around that piece

3184
02:20:21.990 --> 02:20:23.450
is the differentiator.

3185
02:20:23.450 --> 02:20:25.963
Like you have a conscious awareness that,

3186
02:20:27.000 --> 02:20:29.660
a fear like of suddenly,

3187
02:20:29.660 --> 02:20:33.670
kind of moving in that kind of weird guru direction.

3188
02:20:33.670 --> 02:20:35.970
And I don't see that as a threat.

3189
02:20:35.970 --> 02:20:38.500
It just doesn't feel like any part of your sensibility

3190
02:20:38.500 --> 02:20:39.333
whatsoever.

3191
02:20:39.333 --> 02:20:41.000
And what you had said earlier

3192
02:20:42.320 --> 02:20:44.220
was this piece about like thinking about

3193
02:20:44.220 --> 02:20:45.590
how you can be of servicing,

3194
02:20:45.590 --> 02:20:49.030
and like yes, you can be of service in a one-on-one basis

3195
02:20:49.030 --> 02:20:52.520
with that hard case dude or whatever it is.

3196
02:20:52.520 --> 02:20:54.520
But ultimately, like when I look at you

3197
02:20:54.520 --> 02:20:57.740
and I think about service more broadly,

3198
02:20:57.740 --> 02:20:59.610
like what is it about you,

3199
02:20:59.610 --> 02:21:02.040
like what can you do that no one else can do?

3200
02:21:02.040 --> 02:21:03.800
There's other people with tons of money.

3201
02:21:03.800 --> 02:21:06.090
There's other people that have more sobriety than you

3202
02:21:06.090 --> 02:21:07.520
and have been to more rehabs

3203
02:21:07.520 --> 02:21:11.800
and are more steeped in, the literature of psychology.

3204
02:21:11.800 --> 02:21:14.050
The one thing that you have that no one else has

3205
02:21:14.050 --> 02:21:17.190
is this very unique, artistic ability to express yourself

3206
02:21:17.190 --> 02:21:19.410
in a very particular way.

3207
02:21:19.410 --> 02:21:22.130
And for you to channel that in the direction,

3208
02:21:22.130 --> 02:21:25.853
like in this vein of like gratitude and service

3209
02:21:25.853 --> 02:21:29.270
and kind of raising the bar on the kind of conversations

3210
02:21:29.270 --> 02:21:31.490
that we can have so we can help each other

3211
02:21:31.490 --> 02:21:32.340
and heal each other.

3212
02:21:32.340 --> 02:21:33.920
Like that's a gift, man.

3213
02:21:33.920 --> 02:21:37.820
And that's why I think the show is a reflection

3214
02:21:37.820 --> 02:21:40.250
of your very particular sensibility.

3215
02:21:40.250 --> 02:21:44.890
But to me, it's coming from that place.

3216
02:21:44.890 --> 02:21:47.240
And personally, like, selfishly,

3217
02:21:47.240 --> 02:21:49.770
like I wanna see you do more of that

3218
02:21:49.770 --> 02:21:51.970
because that's something nobody else can do.

3219
02:21:53.400 --> 02:21:56.150
Do you wanna see me do more of that

3220
02:21:56.150 --> 02:21:57.800
or would you like to participate in that?

3221
02:21:57.800 --> 02:21:59.330
Well, no, what I'm saying is,

3222
02:21:59.330 --> 02:22:02.530
I want you to embrace that aspect of who you are

3223
02:22:02.530 --> 02:22:04.313
rather than resist it.

3224
02:22:05.450 --> 02:22:06.620
I guess my...

3225
02:22:06.620 --> 02:22:08.480
And to do it like with everything that you've learned

3226
02:22:08.480 --> 02:22:10.450
about where your ego sits

3227
02:22:10.450 --> 02:22:12.910
and what your relationship to it is

3228
02:22:12.910 --> 02:22:15.190
so that you don't succumb

3229
02:22:15.190 --> 02:22:17.750
to some of the things that Tony did

3230
02:22:17.750 --> 02:22:20.300
or fall prey to workaholism and the like,

3231
02:22:20.300 --> 02:22:22.183
because you've got that recovery (indistinct).

3232
02:22:22.183 --> 02:22:24.740
But that's also the thing is recognizing

3233
02:22:24.740 --> 02:22:26.260
I'm not beyond that.

3234
02:22:26.260 --> 02:22:27.220
Just because I'm healthy now,

3235
02:22:27.220 --> 02:22:28.700
doesn't mean I couldn't fall back into that.

3236
02:22:28.700 --> 02:22:30.480
Sure. But it's an opportunity for you

3237
02:22:30.480 --> 02:22:33.300
to reframe your relationship with what you do

3238
02:22:33.300 --> 02:22:34.530
and do it in a healthy way,

3239
02:22:34.530 --> 02:22:36.587
rather than just create a boundary and say,

3240
02:22:36.587 --> 02:22:38.647
"I'm not gonna do it because it's too treacherous

3241
02:22:38.647 --> 02:22:40.560
"or dangerous."

3242
02:22:40.560 --> 02:22:42.523
Like is that a possibility for you?

3243
02:22:44.920 --> 02:22:46.160
I feel like, as they say,

3244
02:22:46.160 --> 02:22:48.000
you peel back the layers of the onion.

3245
02:22:48.000 --> 02:22:51.020
I feel like today I'm not in crisis

3246
02:22:51.020 --> 02:22:54.230
of all the things that used to plague me

3247
02:22:54.230 --> 02:22:59.120
and the like kind of final boss is the workaholism.

3248
02:22:59.120 --> 02:23:02.466
There is a side of me that loves to numb out

3249
02:23:02.466 --> 02:23:06.800
and of course, in the spirit of helping people, right?

3250
02:23:06.800 --> 02:23:09.890
To spend less time with my family and my friends

3251
02:23:09.890 --> 02:23:11.340
and everything.

3252
02:23:11.340 --> 02:23:15.010
And I have like an amazing, what I,

3253
02:23:15.010 --> 02:23:16.330
if you talk to me seven years ago,

3254
02:23:16.330 --> 02:23:21.080
would consider a very boring life, but it's a purposeful,

3255
02:23:21.080 --> 02:23:22.083
meaningful life.

3256
02:23:24.100 --> 02:23:25.700
There's times where things are hectic,

3257
02:23:25.700 --> 02:23:29.639
but it's a pretty like mellow life in that.

3258
02:23:29.639 --> 02:23:33.163
There's something deep in within me that's like,

3259
02:23:34.100 --> 02:23:34.933
why are you gonna sleep right now?

3260
02:23:34.933 --> 02:23:37.140
There's so much more energy,

3261
02:23:37.140 --> 02:23:39.660
you can pull an all nighter right now.

3262
02:23:39.660 --> 02:23:42.710
Well, you know now that you won't be present for your family

3263
02:23:42.710 --> 02:23:43.920
the next day then,

3264
02:23:43.920 --> 02:23:46.780
but you can work on so many projects right now.

3265
02:23:46.780 --> 02:23:48.310
You know you have that capability,

3266
02:23:48.310 --> 02:23:50.460
like that's my iron man, right?

3267
02:23:50.460 --> 02:23:53.420
I can not sleep, no coffee, no drugs

3268
02:23:53.420 --> 02:23:56.997
and work on 30 projects and start an art show

3269
02:23:56.997 --> 02:23:59.870
and an immersive experience and develop other,

3270
02:23:59.870 --> 02:24:03.843
I can do that, and just in the same way.

3271
02:24:05.989 --> 02:24:08.270
Like most of those interviews on my show

3272
02:24:08.270 --> 02:24:09.270
are from two years ago,

3273
02:24:09.270 --> 02:24:11.564
that's how long it took to get that show on to TV.

3274
02:24:11.564 --> 02:24:14.250
It took more work to get that on the TV

3275
02:24:14.250 --> 02:24:16.210
than to actually make the show.

3276
02:24:16.210 --> 02:24:19.157
And what happens when you put the show out, people go,

3277
02:24:19.157 --> 02:24:20.817
"When's the next season?"

3278
02:24:20.817 --> 02:24:24.608
I'm like, I worked on that with Pako

3279
02:24:24.608 --> 02:24:25.980
and the guys from the Philippines.

3280
02:24:25.980 --> 02:24:29.330
I mean, I know it's not the way you do normal TV,

3281
02:24:29.330 --> 02:24:31.870
but we did something on every frame of that.

3282
02:24:31.870 --> 02:24:35.760
Like there's so much stuff that we put in there subliminally

3283
02:24:35.760 --> 02:24:39.262
and hidden messages and stuff that,

3284
02:24:39.262 --> 02:24:40.370
there was a lot of thought put into it.

3285
02:24:40.370 --> 02:24:42.190
And people to go, someone's like,

3286
02:24:42.190 --> 02:24:44.510
I'm like, how about sit with the thing that we made?

3287
02:24:44.510 --> 02:24:46.580
And like is one season enough?

3288
02:24:46.580 --> 02:24:48.130
Does there have to be a season two

3289
02:24:48.130 --> 02:24:50.270
and these types of things?

3290
02:24:50.270 --> 02:24:54.880
So, I'm impulsive,

3291
02:24:54.880 --> 02:24:57.960
I like to just make decisions without thinking about it

3292
02:24:57.960 --> 02:25:01.220
and to, once again,

3293
02:25:01.220 --> 02:25:02.860
that whole thing with like waiting in line,

3294
02:25:02.860 --> 02:25:03.920
like I don't like waiting.

3295
02:25:03.920 --> 02:25:05.280
I don't like sitting in silence.

3296
02:25:05.280 --> 02:25:07.703
I have to just run.

3297
02:25:07.703 --> 02:25:09.230
I have to just get to the next thing.

3298
02:25:09.230 --> 02:25:14.230
So, to sit here and be like, like you said,

3299
02:25:14.370 --> 02:25:17.903
all this reframing and remeasuring these things,

3300
02:25:18.800 --> 02:25:23.800
because I did a show in office building

3301
02:25:24.290 --> 02:25:26.360
about three, four years ago

3302
02:25:26.360 --> 02:25:31.360
where I had to fight against my ego and tell people,

3303
02:25:31.830 --> 02:25:33.499
you can't bring your phone in.

3304
02:25:33.499 --> 02:25:34.647
And I was like,

3305
02:25:34.647 --> 02:25:36.410
"Well, then how are people going to see it online?"

3306
02:25:36.410 --> 02:25:37.837
And I was like,

3307
02:25:37.837 --> 02:25:39.287
"Well, maybe just the people that come see it,

3308
02:25:39.287 --> 02:25:40.583
"that's enough."

3309
02:25:40.583 --> 02:25:45.583
And the other thing is,

3310
02:25:45.910 --> 02:25:48.120
can you really experience something truly

3311
02:25:48.120 --> 02:25:50.610
when there's thousands of people coming through there?

3312
02:25:50.610 --> 02:25:53.370
So, I limited it to groups of seven,

3313
02:25:53.370 --> 02:25:55.380
and then you went in through the whole show

3314
02:25:55.380 --> 02:25:56.740
with like a guide.

3315
02:25:56.740 --> 02:25:59.120
And I implemented like all these things that I learned.

3316
02:25:59.120 --> 02:26:01.960
And I was part of the show too.

3317
02:26:01.960 --> 02:26:06.480
And it was the first phase of the "Choe Show."

3318
02:26:06.480 --> 02:26:11.480
And I had no idea how much that was gonna take out of me,

3319
02:26:13.610 --> 02:26:16.080
like physically and spirit, like emotionally,

3320
02:26:16.080 --> 02:26:19.770
'cause at the end of the day,

3321
02:26:19.770 --> 02:26:23.150
we had a hundred people a day coming in through the show

3322
02:26:23.150 --> 02:26:25.250
when we could have had thousands.

3323
02:26:25.250 --> 02:26:29.940
And I had a staff of like hundreds of people,

3324
02:26:29.940 --> 02:26:32.860
like this is just financially not viable

3325
02:26:32.860 --> 02:26:35.020
in a treatment center, right?

3326
02:26:35.020 --> 02:26:36.410
Like if you went to a treatment center

3327
02:26:36.410 --> 02:26:40.653
and you have like a few therapists and you have your group,

3328
02:26:40.653 --> 02:26:44.270
like I had a team of like hundreds of people

3329
02:26:44.270 --> 02:26:46.090
catering to just you,

3330
02:26:46.090 --> 02:26:49.470
and some of these people would just be on the floor

3331
02:26:49.470 --> 02:26:50.950
crying all night.

3332
02:26:50.950 --> 02:26:55.490
So, I had to find therapists to treat the staff after and...

3333
02:26:55.490 --> 02:26:57.820
Meaning somebody comes in for this experience

3334
02:26:57.820 --> 02:27:00.850
and they're exposed to some form of...

3335
02:27:00.850 --> 02:27:02.167
Yeah, you would fill out an...

3336
02:27:02.167 --> 02:27:04.227
Some version of what you experienced in treatment, right?

3337
02:27:04.227 --> 02:27:06.480
Yeah, and I went for years.

3338
02:27:06.480 --> 02:27:09.450
And I go people aren't gonna take years off to do this.

3339
02:27:09.450 --> 02:27:12.203
So, I'm gonna try to fit it into a four-hour experience.

3340
02:27:12.203 --> 02:27:17.203
And it was, I mean, it floored me.

3341
02:27:17.860 --> 02:27:21.420
It took so much out of me

3342
02:27:21.420 --> 02:27:25.979
and yet the show cost me a tremendous amount of money.

3343
02:27:25.979 --> 02:27:27.930
And I could have monetized it.

3344
02:27:27.930 --> 02:27:29.160
I could have charged people

3345
02:27:29.160 --> 02:27:31.190
and people would have gladly paid.

3346
02:27:31.190 --> 02:27:32.893
And after the show,

3347
02:27:34.300 --> 02:27:38.290
there's a guy who lent me use of the building for free.

3348
02:27:38.290 --> 02:27:39.410
And he's a billionaire.

3349
02:27:39.410 --> 02:27:41.330
And when I told him

3350
02:27:41.330 --> 02:27:43.847
originally what I was gonna use the show for, he's like,

3351
02:27:43.847 --> 02:27:45.477
"Dave, I liked that you're giving back

3352
02:27:45.477 --> 02:27:47.130
"and I'm gonna give you a great price."

3353
02:27:47.130 --> 02:27:48.747
And I was like,

3354
02:27:48.747 --> 02:27:50.210
"I want you to just give it to me for free."

3355
02:27:50.210 --> 02:27:52.260
He's like, "That's not how business works."

3356
02:27:52.260 --> 02:27:55.320
You don't just, I go, "Well, you're rich and I'm rich."

3357
02:27:55.320 --> 02:27:57.920
And why don't you just, like I just told you,

3358
02:27:57.920 --> 02:27:59.100
I'm doing this to help people.

3359
02:27:59.100 --> 02:28:02.040
And he's like, "I like how blunt you are."

3360
02:28:02.040 --> 02:28:05.730
Okay. So, he let me use that building for free.

3361
02:28:05.730 --> 02:28:08.230
And at the end of it, his entire family had gone through.

3362
02:28:08.230 --> 02:28:09.657
And he's like, "When you were explaining it to me,

3363
02:28:09.657 --> 02:28:10.490
"I didn't get it.

3364
02:28:10.490 --> 02:28:11.647
"But now that we've gone through

3365
02:28:11.647 --> 02:28:15.077
"and I've seen it bring my family closer together,

3366
02:28:15.077 --> 02:28:16.757
"let's take this show on the road.

3367
02:28:16.757 --> 02:28:17.848
"I got buildings..."

3368
02:28:17.848 --> 02:28:18.957
He's a real estate guy.

3369
02:28:18.957 --> 02:28:22.320
"I got buildings in every city in the world."

3370
02:28:22.320 --> 02:28:26.620
And so my workaholism goes, this is gonna be a hit show,

3371
02:28:26.620 --> 02:28:27.560
like let's...

3372
02:28:27.560 --> 02:28:29.181
And I had to sit there,

3373
02:28:29.181 --> 02:28:31.940
it's almost embarrassing to say,

3374
02:28:31.940 --> 02:28:35.390
it took like seven people in my life to like sit me down

3375
02:28:35.390 --> 02:28:38.557
and be like, "Look at how messed up you are right now.

3376
02:28:38.557 --> 02:28:42.267
"You just put everything into helping and entertaining

3377
02:28:42.267 --> 02:28:44.447
"and doing all this stuff for these people.

3378
02:28:44.447 --> 02:28:46.947
"And you have to respect what a psychic toll

3379
02:28:46.947 --> 02:28:48.227
"that took on you.

3380
02:28:48.227 --> 02:28:50.867
"And so, we get it that you can like disassociate

3381
02:28:50.867 --> 02:28:52.157
"and just take this show on the road

3382
02:28:52.157 --> 02:28:53.787
"for the next couple of years.

3383
02:28:53.787 --> 02:28:57.917
"But with all the things you learned,

3384
02:28:57.917 --> 02:28:59.970
"can you be kind to yourself?"

3385
02:28:59.970 --> 02:29:01.040
'Cause I don't even know what that means.

3386
02:29:01.040 --> 02:29:04.080
'Cause my whole life, I've treated myself the same way.

3387
02:29:04.080 --> 02:29:07.330
Like if I think about the most verbally

3388
02:29:07.330 --> 02:29:09.320
and physically abusive girlfriends I've had,

3389
02:29:09.320 --> 02:29:10.680
that's how I treat myself.

3390
02:29:10.680 --> 02:29:13.640
I talk down to myself. I say I'm no good.

3391
02:29:13.640 --> 02:29:15.350
And so, I don't wanna sit in that.

3392
02:29:15.350 --> 02:29:20.350
So I go, "So me taking a vacation after this

3393
02:29:20.387 --> 02:29:22.620
"would be kind to myself?"

3394
02:29:22.620 --> 02:29:23.987
And they're like, "Yeah.

3395
02:29:23.987 --> 02:29:25.960
"Like you just did a lot of heavy lifting."

3396
02:29:25.960 --> 02:29:29.777
But in my mind I go, "But it was only 2000 people.

3397
02:29:29.777 --> 02:29:32.320
"It should have been, you know, 200,000 people."

3398
02:29:32.320 --> 02:29:36.760
And it's always that, it's like I wanna help everyone.

3399
02:29:36.760 --> 02:29:38.460
And as long as I'm helping people,

3400
02:29:38.460 --> 02:29:40.200
I never have to help myself.

3401
02:29:40.200 --> 02:29:42.320
I can focus on helping everyone, but myself.

3402
02:29:42.320 --> 02:29:46.182
It just becomes a way to avoid or deflect

3403
02:29:46.182 --> 02:29:48.780
that piece that's the hardest,

3404
02:29:48.780 --> 02:29:50.800
which is learning to love yourself.

3405
02:29:50.800 --> 02:29:54.106
Yeah. And yeah, it was...

3406
02:29:54.106 --> 02:29:58.420
So, I'm here today and my life's quite simple

3407
02:29:58.420 --> 02:30:03.123
and this is the way recovery was explained to me.

3408
02:30:04.580 --> 02:30:08.480
The concept of getting better is very simple.

3409
02:30:08.480 --> 02:30:09.920
It's not complicated, right?

3410
02:30:09.920 --> 02:30:12.820
I just conscious contact with your higher power,

3411
02:30:12.820 --> 02:30:14.900
service work, blocking your phone,

3412
02:30:14.900 --> 02:30:19.900
like there's action, exercising, eating healthy.

3413
02:30:20.430 --> 02:30:21.500
These are all like,

3414
02:30:21.500 --> 02:30:24.190
none of these are like hard concepts to understand,

3415
02:30:24.190 --> 02:30:25.360
but it's hard.

3416
02:30:25.360 --> 02:30:28.000
It's simple, but it's very hard.

3417
02:30:28.000 --> 02:30:31.372
Like it's gonna take me an incredible amount of willpower

3418
02:30:31.372 --> 02:30:33.230
after this interview to drive home

3419
02:30:33.230 --> 02:30:34.880
without stopping at Burger King.

3420
02:30:34.880 --> 02:30:36.541
Like that's just the truth.

3421
02:30:36.541 --> 02:30:37.374
You want me to give you a ride?

3422
02:30:37.374 --> 02:30:41.090
You can get me to the next exit and then...

3423
02:30:41.090 --> 02:30:42.860
I'll escort you out of here.

3424
02:30:42.860 --> 02:30:44.513
You can do it.

3425
02:30:44.513 --> 02:30:45.346
Thank you.

3426
02:30:45.346 --> 02:30:47.384
You just saying that, like you can do it,

3427
02:30:47.384 --> 02:30:49.350
that's a nice positive step.

3428
02:30:49.350 --> 02:30:51.150
It's definitely within your power.

3429
02:30:52.180 --> 02:30:53.290
Yeah, man.

3430
02:30:53.290 --> 02:30:55.690
I'll let you know if mission accomplished or not.

3431
02:30:55.690 --> 02:30:56.543
We'll see.

3432
02:30:57.380 --> 02:30:59.270
Well, we should round this out,

3433
02:30:59.270 --> 02:31:01.193
but I don't wanna let you go without,

3434
02:31:02.560 --> 02:31:07.560
maybe a few words for the one who still suffers,

3435
02:31:07.560 --> 02:31:09.010
the one being the many,

3436
02:31:09.010 --> 02:31:10.630
because I think there's a lot of people

3437
02:31:10.630 --> 02:31:13.700
who struggle in silence

3438
02:31:13.700 --> 02:31:17.850
with some form of compulsive behavior or addiction

3439
02:31:17.850 --> 02:31:20.020
to substance or process.

3440
02:31:20.020 --> 02:31:20.900
In some way,

3441
02:31:20.900 --> 02:31:25.900
I mean, I just feel like this is the problem of our age.

3442
02:31:26.210 --> 02:31:28.390
Like it's just metastasizing like crazy.

3443
02:31:28.390 --> 02:31:31.810
So, whether it's gambling or food or phones or sex

3444
02:31:31.810 --> 02:31:36.100
or shopping or drugs and alcohol, whatever it is,

3445
02:31:36.100 --> 02:31:39.840
like I feel like almost all of us struggles in one way

3446
02:31:39.840 --> 02:31:42.610
or the other along this very broad spectrum.

3447
02:31:42.610 --> 02:31:47.320
And finding a way out is really hard for most people.

3448
02:31:47.320 --> 02:31:49.800
So, for the one who is still suffering right now,

3449
02:31:49.800 --> 02:31:52.530
I just wanna tell you, once again,

3450
02:31:52.530 --> 02:31:53.900
I don't wanna make it about race,

3451
02:31:53.900 --> 02:31:57.960
but I've been to, you guys have heard me now.

3452
02:31:57.960 --> 02:32:00.650
I've been to all these treatment facilities,

3453
02:32:00.650 --> 02:32:04.541
I've seen in seven years of treatment

3454
02:32:04.541 --> 02:32:06.510
two other Asian people.

3455
02:32:06.510 --> 02:32:08.730
It's not part of our culture.

3456
02:32:08.730 --> 02:32:11.420
And the last one almost threw me out

3457
02:32:11.420 --> 02:32:13.530
'cause it was my voice speaking to me

3458
02:32:13.530 --> 02:32:15.350
in the form of another kid.

3459
02:32:15.350 --> 02:32:18.880
I was at a meeting and a kid came in and he was Korean,

3460
02:32:18.880 --> 02:32:21.579
and he saw me and I could tell right away, he recognized me.

3461
02:32:21.579 --> 02:32:23.757
And at the end of the meeting, he's like.

3462
02:32:23.757 --> 02:32:27.585
"Dave Choe, you're rich. You're famous.

3463
02:32:27.585 --> 02:32:29.500
"What are doing here?"

3464
02:32:29.500 --> 02:32:30.700
Like I wasn't...

3465
02:32:30.700 --> 02:32:32.987
And as he was saying that in my head, I was like,

3466
02:32:32.987 --> 02:32:34.157
"You're right. What am I doing here?

3467
02:32:34.157 --> 02:32:35.620
"I'm better than this."

3468
02:32:35.620 --> 02:32:37.160
And that almost took me out.

3469
02:32:37.160 --> 02:32:38.737
I was like, "I don't need to be here.

3470
02:32:38.737 --> 02:32:40.790
"I am better than these people."

3471
02:32:40.790 --> 02:32:44.690
So, if you're listening now and, no judging,

3472
02:32:44.690 --> 02:32:49.690
I don't care what video games, porn, the internet,

3473
02:32:49.730 --> 02:32:54.460
YouTube, binge watching TV, food, whatever your thing is,

3474
02:32:54.460 --> 02:32:55.393
no judging.

3475
02:32:56.340 --> 02:32:58.670
The same brain that got you into this mess

3476
02:32:58.670 --> 02:33:01.350
is not the one that's gonna get you out.

3477
02:33:01.350 --> 02:33:05.780
You need a hand, and all those tools, all these electronics,

3478
02:33:05.780 --> 02:33:07.420
all these things that are used for evil

3479
02:33:07.420 --> 02:33:11.660
and to numb you and distract you,

3480
02:33:11.660 --> 02:33:13.800
you can use those same tools to...

3481
02:33:14.848 --> 02:33:16.680
I've been to these places that cost money,

3482
02:33:16.680 --> 02:33:18.920
but there's so much free services.

3483
02:33:18.920 --> 02:33:22.499
There's literally a 12-step program for every addiction.

3484
02:33:22.499 --> 02:33:26.310
And if you think you are any of these things, you just,

3485
02:33:26.310 --> 02:33:27.220
am I workaholic?

3486
02:33:27.220 --> 02:33:29.330
Just type in characteristics of a workaholic.

3487
02:33:29.330 --> 02:33:31.533
And you'll see if you are very quickly.

3488
02:33:32.560 --> 02:33:35.660
You probably are because we live in a nation,

3489
02:33:35.660 --> 02:33:38.157
everyone goes, "Hey, America is a nation of immigrants,

3490
02:33:38.157 --> 02:33:38.990
"right?"

3491
02:33:38.990 --> 02:33:41.430
But all that means is we're a nation of workaholics

3492
02:33:41.430 --> 02:33:44.950
because everyone came here for something better

3493
02:33:44.950 --> 02:33:46.750
and that means work your ass off.

3494
02:33:46.750 --> 02:33:48.120
So even if you're not a workaholic,

3495
02:33:48.120 --> 02:33:49.683
your family's workaholic.

3496
02:33:50.780 --> 02:33:52.793
And all these things,

3497
02:33:54.023 --> 02:33:58.200
it's not gonna be you on your phone alone,

3498
02:33:58.200 --> 02:34:01.020
watching porn alone, playing video games alone,

3499
02:34:01.020 --> 02:34:02.420
it's through connection.

3500
02:34:02.420 --> 02:34:06.693
And so, reach out, ask for help, tell someone.

3501
02:34:10.330 --> 02:34:11.787
When you ask anyone in society,

3502
02:34:11.787 --> 02:34:13.320
"Hey, man, how are you doing?"

3503
02:34:13.320 --> 02:34:14.670
Most people will give you the answer,

3504
02:34:14.670 --> 02:34:16.340
Fine, good. Okay.

3505
02:34:16.340 --> 02:34:18.200
All of which aren't emotions.

3506
02:34:18.200 --> 02:34:20.550
that's our automatic response.

3507
02:34:20.550 --> 02:34:21.383
I'm okay.

3508
02:34:21.383 --> 02:34:22.750
I mean, you could have the worst thing happening

3509
02:34:22.750 --> 02:34:24.920
in your life today and be like, "I'm fine. I'm okay."

3510
02:34:24.920 --> 02:34:29.920
So, just, it's okay. You're not okay.

3511
02:34:32.206 --> 02:34:35.800
And that doesn't mean like you're not gonna be okay forever.

3512
02:34:35.800 --> 02:34:36.760
You just ask for help.

3513
02:34:36.760 --> 02:34:37.950
There's support.

3514
02:34:37.950 --> 02:34:41.200
And as someone, my life today,

3515
02:34:41.200 --> 02:34:43.141
I can't get through it without this.

3516
02:34:43.141 --> 02:34:44.950
I'm part of a men's group.

3517
02:34:44.950 --> 02:34:47.920
I go to 12-step meetings regularly on Zoom,

3518
02:34:47.920 --> 02:34:49.920
which is the easiest it's ever been.

3519
02:34:49.920 --> 02:34:51.430
There's kind of a disconnect with the Zoom,

3520
02:34:51.430 --> 02:34:53.330
but still better than nothing.

3521
02:34:53.330 --> 02:34:55.290
I have a therapist that I see

3522
02:34:55.290 --> 02:34:58.380
and it's like there's a part of my addict brain

3523
02:34:58.380 --> 02:34:59.213
that's like,

3524
02:35:00.777 --> 02:35:03.537
"You need to go talk to someone once a week for an hour

3525
02:35:03.537 --> 02:35:04.840
"about..."

3526
02:35:04.840 --> 02:35:05.717
And I go,

3527
02:35:05.717 --> 02:35:08.857
"Do you know how much time I spend in casinos

3528
02:35:08.857 --> 02:35:11.707
"and at strip clubs and like all these places,

3529
02:35:11.707 --> 02:35:15.800
"like I can't spend one hour a week on myself?"

3530
02:35:15.800 --> 02:35:20.540
So, there's help out there. It's not hopeless.

3531
02:35:20.540 --> 02:35:24.740
And I wish for all my friends that killed themselves

3532
02:35:24.740 --> 02:35:27.790
and for the times in my life where I contemplated suicide

3533
02:35:27.790 --> 02:35:32.790
and I mean, we live in a society where it's normalized,

3534
02:35:32.810 --> 02:35:35.800
where it's more okay to kill yourself than to ask for help.

3535
02:35:35.800 --> 02:35:37.450
That's where we're at now.

3536
02:35:37.450 --> 02:35:40.257
